{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-vacuum-state","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:vacuum-state","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence and Uniqueness of the Vacuum State","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-direct-limit-algebra","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-gauge-group","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-descent"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-vacuum-state"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-vacuum-state-su2"],"tags":["vacuum-state","invariant","frobenius-trace"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Torsion.invariant_functional_unique","text":"vacuum-state.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/vacuum-state.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:vacuum-state\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a <a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\">quantum observable universe</a>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> denote the substrate parameter. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{A}_\\infty</code> be its <a href=\"#def:direct-limit-algebra\">direct limit algebra</a>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_q = \\mathrm{Aut}^{\\otimes}(\\tau)</code> be the <a href=\"#def:quantum-gauge-group\">quantum gauge group</a>, acting on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{A}_\\infty</code> by conjugation. There exists a unique <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-linear functional <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi \\colon \\mathcal{A}_\\infty \\to R</code> that is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_q</code>-invariant:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\varphi(g \\cdot a) = \\varphi(a)\n  \\quad\\text{for all } g \\in G_q,\n  a \\in \\mathcal{A}_\\infty.</code></pre>\n<p>In the archimedean realisation, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_q = \\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi</code> is the unique <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SU}(2)</code>-invariant state on the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C^*</code>-algebraic direct limit.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/vacuum-state.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"5.6.6"}
